      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Simplify cost labels and clarify estimate provenance",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nSimplify cost navigation labels and move the general cost explanation from the menu into Cost settings.\n\n- Rename provider cost buttons and sections to the consistent label `Cost`\n- Move the general reported-versus-estimated explanation to the bottom of Cost settings\n- Keep one short Codex-specific note beside its displayed values:\n  `Estimated from token usage · not a subscription bill`\n- Show that note directly below `Est. total` inside the Codex Cost submenu so submenu-only layouts retain the estimate context\n- Remove repeated explanations and obsolete localized labels from menu and chart views\n- Keep the CLI label explicit because CLI output has no surrounding UI context\n\n## Why\n\nThe previous menu mixed navigation labels with explanations such as “API-equivalent estimate” and “Token-based cost estimate.” This caused three problems:\n\n1. The labels were long and frequently truncated.\n2. The same Cost destination had different names depending on the provider.\n3. A single estimate-focused label was not accurate for every provider: some costs are provider-reported, while others are calculated from token usage.\n\nA button should clearly describe where it leads, so all provider buttons now use the concise label `Cost`.\n\nMoving the general explanation out of the menu also lets cost entries with submenus use a standard native menu row instead of a custom multi-line SwiftUI card. This restores consistent menu sizing, highlighting, and interaction behavior.\n\nThe general explanation applies to the Cost feature as a whole, not to one menu item. It now appears in Cost settings, where users can see that values may be provider-reported or estimated from token usage at public API prices, and that estimates are not subscription charges.\n\nCodex keeps a short explanation next to its displayed values because its prominent dollar amounts are token-derived and could otherwise be mistaken for an actual bill. It appears under the inline dashboard details and directly below the estimated total in the Cost submenu, preserving the necessary context without bringing the long explanation back to the parent menu row.\n\nThe CLI retains `Codex token-based cost` because terminal output must explain itself without relying on the menu or settings UI.\n\n## Result\n\nThe menu is shorter and more consistent, while the distinction between reported costs, token-derived estimates, and subscription billing remains available where users need it.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Focused cost, menu, settings, CLI, and localization tests: 134 passed\n- Final Codex submenu update: all 28 `CostHistoryChartMenuViewTests` passed\n- `make check`\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n- Manually verified the complete change set in the app, including the native Cost row, Cost settings explanation, inline Codex estimate hint, and the Codex submenu note below `Est. total`\n\n## Screenshot\nbefore\n<img width=\"308\" height=\"268\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-17 at 11 32 38 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f757b3d8-4ca8-428b-a927-9d41770dab4a\" />\n\nafter\n<img width=\"309\" height=\"180\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-18 at 3 33 15 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2add4941-c7e4-45f1-8003-e715de5ca31f\" />\n",
